linux user who can log into serverr and has limited access only to view tomcat logs

1. create user
  > sudo adduser tomcatloguser

2. set password
  > passwd tomcatloguser
      //give password

3. to remove user from sudo group()red hat-based system
  > sudo usermod -G "" tomcatloguser

  to check group membership
  > groups tomcatloguser

4. set read-only access to logs directory
  > sudo setfacl -m u:tomcatloguser:rx /opt/tomcatDir/logs
  > sudo setfacl -R -m u:tomcatloguser:r /opt/tomcatDir/logs /*

this allows user to
  -> enter logs directory
  -> read log files (ex. catalina.out)

5. log in as user
  > su - tomcatloguser
  > cd /opt/tomcatDir/logs
  > less catalina.out
  
